{"id":"R0074","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed 2026 Drones article evaluating Orion collaborative LLM inference across a multi-UAV testbed.","e":{"E1":["T",3,"1. Introduction","we propose Orion, a novel collaborative inference framework","Primary research article proposing an edge-only collaborative LLM inference framework.","PDF"],"E2":["T",14,"4.1. Experimental Setup","Our experimental testbed comprises five heterogeneous devices: three NVIDIA AGX Orin modules","Evaluated swarm includes three AGX Orin and one Orin NX UAV nodes.","PDF"],"E3":["T",6,"3. Proposed Solution: The Orion Framework","Optimal LLM Partitioning (Section 3.1), which determines the layer-to-device mapping to minimize stage bottlenecks","LLM layers and input sequences are partitioned across UAV nodes for collaborative inference.","PDF"],"E4":["T",16,"4.2. Latency on Llama-2 Models of Varying Scales","For the 7B model, Orion achieved a latency of 8864 ms","Simulation evaluates Llama-2 7B, 13B, and 70B prefill latency against five baselines.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Article metadata","Accepted: 21 May 2026 Published: 26 May 2026","Published 26 May 2026, within the 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",2,"1. Introduction","Unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) swarms are increasingly deployed for real-time surveillance","Full 26-page article is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Article metadata","Revised: 15 May 2026 Accepted: 21 May 2026","Peer-reviewed MDPI Drones article (revised/accepted) with DP partitioning method and Llama-2 simulation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0075","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","primary":"","reason":"Awaiting classification because the 2026 IEEE Internet of Things Journal Early Access PDF lacks a verifiable online publication date at or before 2026-11-26.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","This paper presents CIDER, a collaborative multi-exit inference framework","Primary research article proposing the CIDER collaborative multi-exit inference framework.","PDF"],"E2":["T",11,"IV-C. Parameter Analysis","we evaluate different swarm configurations by varying the number of deployed student models","Evaluated multi-UAV setting varies swarm size from 2 to 5 UAVs (Table IV).","PDF"],"E3":["T",4,"III-A. Task Definition","Assistant UAVs process local student branches and selectively transmit intermediate features","Multi-exit student models are partitioned across Assistant and Master UAVs with feature fusion.","PDF"],"E4":["T",10,"IV-B. Results Analysis","On CIFAR-10, CIDER attains 89.09% accuracy with 17.91 ms computation","Hardware-profiled simulation on Jetson TX2 reports CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100 accuracy and latency.","PDF"],"E5":["U",0,"Citation information / Publisher metadata","","PDF shows Early Access copyright 2026 and download date 2026-11-25 without publication date; publisher/Crossref date unavailable.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. Introduction","This challenge becomes particularly pronounced in Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) networks","Full 15-page manuscript is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","This article has been accepted for publication in IEEE Internet of Things Journal","Peer-reviewed IEEE Internet of Things Journal accepted article with distillation/LinUCB method and CIFAR-10/100 results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0081","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","primary":"","reason":"Awaiting classification because the MobiSys 2022 Call for Demos classifies this 2-page demo as an extended abstract selected by audience interest without confirming peer review.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","This demonstration shows a working prototype of IDEA","Primary system prototype report describing the IDEA multi-UAV collaborative inference system.","PDF"],"E2":["T",2,"3 DEMONSTRATION & RESULTS","we have implemented IDEA on three self-constructed real-world UAVs","Evaluated on three real-world UAVs (one master UAV and two worker UAVs).","PDF"],"E3":["T",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","IDEA splits the model (e.g., convolutional neural networks (CNN)) into three different submodels","Faster R-CNN is split into three submodels and executed in pipeline across three UAVs.","PDF"],"E4":["T",2,"3 DEMONSTRATION & RESULTS","IDEA maintains higher frame rate than single UAV all the time","Evaluates Faster R-CNN over 100 frames, reporting ~2.6x frame rate improvement over single UAV.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"ACM Reference Format","MobiSys '22), June 25-July 1, 2022, Portland, OR, USA","Published at MobiSys 2022 (June 25-July 1, 2022), within the eligible date window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","Recently, unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs)-based object detection has emerged as a promising way","Full 2-page report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["U",0,"Call for Demos","A demo/video submission requires an extended abstract no longer than two 8.5x11-inch pages","MobiSys 2022 Call for Demos classifies it as an extended abstract selected by audience interest without confirming peer review, though method and 100-frame results are reported.","https://www.sigmobile.org/mobisys/2022/demos.html"]}}
{"id":"R0083","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed 2025 Internet of Things research article evaluating containerized DNN partitioning across UAV swarms.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Article header","Research article Distributed inference in IoT-based aerial network of UAVs","Primary research article proposing a distributed DNN partition deployment method.","PDF"],"E2":["T",7,"4.2. Simulation results","e2e latency using 10 UAVs in two different deployment areas","Evaluated in simulations with 5 to 20 UAVs (10 UAVs in Fig. 3).","PDF"],"E3":["T",3,"3.1.2. Deployment process","center UAV partitions and containerizes the requested DNN into the Containerized Partition Table","AlexNet and VGG19 are partitioned into containers and deployed across worker UAVs for inference.","PDF"],"E4":["T",7,"4.2. Simulation results","our proposed method is able to obtain the lowest e2e latency","Simulations compare end-to-end latency and energy per device against NN, HRE, and LO baselines.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Article info","Accepted 17 December 2024 Available online 3 January 2025","Available online 3 January 2025, within the 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1. Introduction","Interest in unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) is on the rise","Full 10-page article is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Article info","Received 12 November 2024; Received in revised form 13 December 2024","Peer-reviewed Elsevier Internet of Things research article with partition algorithm and simulation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0089","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed 2023 Physical Communication article evaluating split early-exit DNN inference across drones and aerial servers.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Article header","Full length article A hybrid fast inference approach with distributed neural networks","Primary research article proposing a hybrid early-exit and offloading inference framework.","PDF"],"E2":["T",8,"5. Simulation and numerical results","The simulation scenario includes 4 edge servers with 12 drone terminals","Evaluated with 12 drone terminals and 4 aerial computing edge servers.","PDF"],"E3":["T",5,"3.3. Model training","deploy the shallow network at the drone terminals, and the entire network at the edge servers","ResNet/Branchy DNN is split between drone terminals (10-layer head) and aerial servers (22-layer tail).","PDF"],"E4":["T",8,"5. Simulation and numerical results","We train our model with the CIFAR data set","PyTorch simulations on CIFAR-10 evaluate upload ratio and system accuracy against AL, AO, and RS.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Article history","Accepted 17 June 2023 Available online 24 June 2023","Available online 24 June 2023, within the 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1. Introduction","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), driven by the development of automation","Full 12-page article is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Article history","Received 31 March 2023 Received in revised form 31 May 2023","Peer-reviewed Elsevier Physical Communication full-length article with hybrid inference method and CIFAR-10 results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0092","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","primary":"","reason":"Awaiting classification because the 2026 IEEE Internet of Things Journal Early Access PDF lacks a verifiable online publication date at or before 2026-11-26.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose DDCI, a decentralized collaborative inference framework","Primary research article proposing the DDCI decentralized collaborative inference framework.","PDF"],"E2":["T",10,"V-A. Simulation Setup","The swarm comprises N=10 UAVs with heterogeneous compute capacities","Evaluated in a 10-UAV swarm (scaled N=6 to 20 in Fig. 5a).","PDF"],"E3":["T",5,"III-E.1. DNN Model Partitioning","We consider layer-wise partitioning of a DNN with L layers","Each UAV selects a neighbor via DRL and splits VGG-16/19, YOLOv5m, or GoogLeNet-22 in a MiniBatch pipeline.","PDF"],"E4":["T",10,"V-D. Multi-Network Performance Comparison","Table V presents results across four DNN architectures","Evaluates P50 latency, deadline satisfaction, and energy over 30 episodes with Wilcoxon tests.","PDF"],"E5":["U",0,"Citation information / Publisher metadata","","PDF shows Early Access copyright 2026 and download date 2026-11-25 without publication date; publisher/Crossref date unavailable.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. Introduction","The rapid advancement of unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) technology has enabled","Full 16-page manuscript is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","This article has been accepted for publication in IEEE Internet of Things Journal","Peer-reviewed IEEE Internet of Things Journal accepted article with DDCI method and 4-DNN simulation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0095","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed 2026 Ad Hoc Networks article evaluating PPO-based DNN macro-block partitioning and caching across UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","we propose a multi-UAV collaborative inference scheme based on dynamic partitioning","Primary research article proposing the PPO-DMCP collaborative inference and caching scheme.","PDF"],"E2":["T",8,"5.1. Experimental environment and parameter settings","The system consists of a total of N=5 UAVs operating in a two-dimensional area","Evaluated with N=5 UAVs (1 core, 4 computing UAVs), scaled N=2 to 8 in Fig. 12.","PDF"],"E3":["T",4,"3.3. Dynamic model partitioning strategy","the PPO-DMCP agent determines N-1 internal split points to divide the model across N UAVs","DNNs are abstracted into macro-blocks and partitioned across computing UAVs with intermediate feature transmission.","PDF"],"E4":["T",10,"5.4.2. Comparison of partitioning schemes","our proposed PPO-DMCP strategy achieves a 100% completion rate with the lowest total latency","Simulations evaluate latency, completion rate, and caching across Equal, Single, Prop, Layer-PPO, and RL baselines.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Article info","Accepted 8 July 2026 Available online 16 July 2026","Available online 16 July 2026, within the 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1. Introduction","With the rapid evolution of Internet of Vehicles (IoV) and AI","Full 13-page article is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Article info","Received 28 January 2026; Received in revised form 23 June 2026","Peer-reviewed Elsevier Ad Hoc Networks article with PPO-DMCP method and simulation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0108","decision":"EXCLUDE","primary":"E3","reason":"Excluded on E3 because the paper proposes federated learning and generic task offloading without any specified DNN inference partitioning, assignment, or orchestration.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","This paper proposes a Secure and Intelligent Edge Computing Architecture","Primary research article proposing a blockchain- and FL-based edge architecture.","PDF"],"E2":["T",6,"IV. RESULTS AND DISCUSSIONS","Simulation experiments were conducted using a swarm of 50 autonomous drones","Evaluated in a simulation with 10 to 50 autonomous drones (Fig. 4).","PDF"],"E3":["F",5,"III. PROPOSED METHODOLOGY","drones and edge nodes train local machine learning models using their own datasets","Proposes federated learning and generic task offloading without any specified DNN/CNN/VLM/LLM inference partitioning or assignment.","PDF"],"E4":["T",7,"IV. RESULTS AND DISCUSSIONS","Performance metrics including latency, energy consumption, packet delivery ratio, and task completion rate were evaluated","Reports simulation comparisons of latency (Table 1), energy (Table 2), and task completion (Table 3).","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Journal header","Vol 23 Issue 11, NOV, 2023","Published November 2023, within the 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","The rapid advancement of Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) has enabled","Full 9-page article is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",0,"Peer Review Policy","To have been peer-reviewed, a manuscript should have been reviewed by at least one external reviewer","IJESAT states external peer review for original research; PDF contains architecture and simulation results.","https://ijesat.com/ppolicy.php?content_id=11"]}}
{"id":"R0110","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","primary":"","reason":"Awaiting classification because the 2026 IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology Early Access PDF lacks a verifiable online publication date at or before 2026-11-26.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","This paper presents RDI-LLM, a resilient distributed inference framework","Primary research article proposing the RDI-LLM distributed LLM inference framework.","PDF"],"E2":["T",10,"TABLE III","Number of UAVs in the scaling experiments","Table III specifies swarm size N=8-32 UAVs (default N=16 in Table IV).","PDF"],"E3":["T",3,"III-A. Operational Semantics","The FFN of each decoder layer is partitioned into K disjoint shards","Decoder-only LLM FFN shards are redundantly placed on UAVs with online partial activation and aggregation.","PDF"],"E4":["T",12,"V-D. Ablation Study","RDI-LLM completes all 30 missions, as does the recent-framework baseline","Simulations on Llama-2-70B report completion rate, latency, energy, and TTFT against eight baselines.","PDF"],"E5":["U",0,"Citation information / Publisher metadata","","PDF shows manuscript received 2026-02-11, copyright 2026, and download date 2026-11-25 without publication date; publisher/Crossref date unavailable.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","mobile edge intelligence and integrated communication-sensing-computation for 6G are pushing","Full 16-page manuscript is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Header","This article has been accepted for publication in IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology","Peer-reviewed IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology accepted article with A'+E+B method and Llama-2 simulation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0111","decision":"EXCLUDE","primary":"E7","reason":"Excluded on E7 (with secondary failures on E2, E3, and E4) because the report presents only a pre-experiment analysis plan with no reported evaluation results.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"1 Introduction","this paper proposes a systematic method and evaluation platform","Primary research paper proposing a multi-UAV communication coverage method.","PDF"],"E2":["F",4,"6 Results presentation and analysis template","part of the pre-experiment analysis plan and indicator framework; no quantitative conclusions","No evaluated multi-UAV setting exists because no experiments or simulations were executed.","PDF"],"E3":["F",3,"4.4 Edge computing collaboration and consistency","edge modules are deployed on a few core UAVs for local data preprocessing, model inference","Focuses on wide-area communication coverage with MARL and mentions local inference without evaluated distributed DNN inference.","PDF"],"E4":["F",4,"6 Results presentation and analysis template","The above presentation formats and conclusion descriptions are part of the pre-experiment analysis plan","Contains only a pre-experiment analysis plan and indicator template with no evaluation results.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Journal header","2025, VOL. 6, NO. 8, 240-244","Published in 2025, wholly within the 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1 Introduction","In scenarios such as smart cities, emergency rescue, coverage in remote areas","Full 5-page paper is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["F",4,"6 Results presentation and analysis template","no quantitative conclusions beyond the document are introduced. Final values are based on simulation/real-world results","Lacks reported evaluation results (pre-experiment plan only) and PDF lacks peer-review evidence.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0117","decision":"EXCLUDE","primary":"E1","reason":"Excluded on E1 (with secondary failures on E7, E2, E3, and E4) because this is a review paper developing a conceptual reference architecture without experimental evaluation.","e":{"E1":["F",1,"ABSTRACT","This review develops an evidence-based five-layer IoT-AI-UAV swarm reference architecture","Explicitly a review paper synthesizing prior literature into a conceptual reference architecture.","PDF"],"E2":["F",18,"5.5. Architecture Validation through Cross-Literature Evidence","Because the proposed architecture is conceptual rather than experimentally implemented","No multi-UAV system was experimentally or simulation-evaluated; conceptual synthesis only.","PDF"],"E3":["F",22,"6.5. Synthesis of the Study Objectives","The framework should be understood as a conceptual reference architecture derived from the reviewed evidence","No evaluated collaborative DNN inference workload; discusses edge-cloud AI conceptually from literature.","PDF"],"E4":["F",22,"6.5. Synthesis of the Study Objectives","rather than as an experimentally validated operational system","No experiments, simulations, or mathematical performance analysis are reported.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Journal header","Vol. 5, No. 3, September 2026, pp. 21~49","Published September 2026 (Accepted August 27, 2026), within the 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1. INTRODUCTION","Airports are among the most security-sensitive infrastructures in modern transportation systems","Full 29-page article is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["F",18,"5.5. Architecture Validation through Cross-Literature Evidence","its validation is based on cross-literature synthesis","Review article lacking original experimental/simulation evaluation results despite journal acceptance dates.","PDF"]}}
